{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"additional_concerns\":[\"Effective retention has no complete fulfillment test in the supplied passages. Allocation of accountability, supervisory conduct and operational outcomes must remain distinct; neither outsourcing nor an operational failure alone establishes loss of accountability.\",\"The register duties in both supplied versions of clause 6.8 concern specified register keepers; the longer version separately requires disclosure of register addresses on request. Clause 6.11C concerns outsourced valuation. The intermediary issuance and due-diligence provisions have their own activity conditions. None automatically supplies a Product Provider retention test.\",\"Paragraph 14 independently requires confirmation. Footnote 5 specifies minimum compliance with paragraphs 10–13 and high confidence concerning smart-contract vulnerabilities or security flaws. Reading its demonstration language as elaborating the request-triggered duty and reading it as an independent duty remain alternatives; absence of a request does not remove confirmation or underlying responsibilities.\",\"Paragraphs 15 and 16 expressly condition third-party audit or verification and a satisfactory legal opinion on an SFC request. Their absence without a request does not establish noncompliance with those duties or fulfillment of paragraph 10.\",\"Part A of the Tokenised Securities Circular appendix, the applicable portions of Part B, and the full requirements of paragraphs 12–13 are not supplied. They would be needed for a broader applicable-standard or minimum-compliance assessment; no external dependency IDs are available. Actual governance, supervision and operational facts are also absent.\"],\"checks\":[{\"authority\":{\"dependency_ids\":[],\"rationale\":\"The supplied paragraph 10 and footnote 1 establish this responsibility allocation without an additional external dependency. A complete fulfillment standard would require further investigation.\",\"status\":\"NONE_DECLARED\"},\"candidate_id\":\"deferred.1b01f7617ea39afc65a0bb8f\",\"claim_id\":\"claim.0014cf34bf89a0c967381f17\",\"executable_correspondence\":{\"rationale\":\"The candidate is UNENCODED and supplies no executable expressions. Correspondence cannot be assessed despite support for the responsibility duty.\",\"representation_quotes\":[],\"status\":\"UNAVAILABLE\"},\"followup_questions\":[\"What executable scope and result expressions will implement the retained-accountability question?\",\"What applicable standard and actual governance, authority and supervisory evidence distinguish effective retention from formal allocation without treating operational failure alone as loss of accountability?\",\"Can the applicable Part A appendix factors be supplied before constructing a complete fulfillment test?\"],\"question_relation\":{\"evidence\":[{\"span_ids\":[\"span.3087bf463010cb68bcc511470848b1c2fb28940d922f1c568d02245a36b20ce6\"]},{\"span_ids\":[\"span.a59eab21f4264d5af4a3394ecbdcd7bb26a1247f78e28a2ef7b14bf208b230c9\"]}],\"question_hash\":\"09b357c96bbda35011438b9d918abfc4ad160fc16f3e3d8ae1e2c9996fdc17f5\",\"rationale\":\"Retaining ultimate responsibility for management and operational soundness directly forms part of the typed accountability question. The source establishes the duty, but supplies no sufficient test for effective retention or discharge through supervision.\",\"status\":\"RELEVANT\"},\"source_support\":{\"evidence\":[{\"span_ids\":[\"span.3087bf463010cb68bcc511470848b1c2fb28940d922f1c568d02245a36b20ce6\"]},{\"span_ids\":[\"span.a59eab21f4264d5af4a3394ecbdcd7bb26a1247f78e28a2ef7b14bf208b230c9\"]}],\"rationale\":\"Paragraph 10 expressly assigns continuing ultimate responsibility; footnote 1 reinforces full responsibility despite outsourcing. The claim captures the management and operational-soundness portion without negating the separate ownership-record responsibility.\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\"}},{\"authority\":{\"dependency_ids\":[],\"rationale\":\"Paragraph 14 and footnote 5 suffice to establish the stated request-triggered demonstration duty. No additional external authority is necessary for this limited proposition.\",\"status\":\"NONE_DECLARED\"},\"candidate_id\":\"deferred.1b01f7617ea39afc65a0bb8f\",\"claim_id\":\"claim.b8bfeece7669b37ae5c67d5f\",\"executable_correspondence\":{\"rationale\":\"The demonstration duty is outside the typed retained-accountability assessment. This disposition does not establish executable fidelity; the candidate also has no executable meaning.\",\"representation_quotes\":[],\"status\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\"},\"followup_questions\":[\"Should demonstration be assessed in a separate question preserving the request trigger, SFC satisfaction standard and footnote 5 minimum content?\",\"Does footnote 5 elaborate paragraph 14's request-triggered demonstration or independently require demonstration without a request?\"],\"question_relation\":{\"evidence\":[{\"span_ids\":[\"span.d497cf934e7afabd2245d074f95ab09c2f09fad2d5f5eed4bdb2376422d04208\"]},{\"span_ids\":[\"span.e2df1e193fc2c3ac433253055086280251a16d0672c6f0702af0b4fd9f212bfa\"]}],\"question_hash\":\"09b357c96bbda35011438b9d918abfc4ad160fc16f3e3d8ae1e2c9996fdc17f5\",\"rationale\":\"Demonstrating specified matters to the SFC is a separate assurance duty, not the retention of accountability assessed here. Footnote 5 includes paragraph 10 compliance among demonstration content, but that evidential connection does not make demonstration a necessary or sufficient retention test.\",\"status\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE_TO_THIS_QUESTION\"},\"source_support\":{\"evidence\":[{\"span_ids\":[\"span.d497cf934e7afabd2245d074f95ab09c2f09fad2d5f5eed4bdb2376422d04208\"]},{\"span_ids\":[\"span.e2df1e193fc2c3ac433253055086280251a16d0672c6f0702af0b4fd9f212bfa\"]}],\"rationale\":\"Paragraph 14 expressly supports demonstration upon request to the SFC's satisfaction of all three stated matters. Footnote 5 adds minimum content and repeats demonstration without the trigger. Both readings support the duty when requested; neither supports treating this claim as establishing that demonstration is required only upon request.\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\"}}]}"}}
